---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Financial | BeaconGuard Authorization for Consequential AI Actions"
  description="BeaconGuard independently authorizes consequential AI-assisted financial actions before execution while preserving analyst, compliance, and system-of-record authority."
>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <p class="section-label">FINANCIAL SERVICES</p>
    <h1>Authorize customer-impacting AI actions before they execute</h1>
    <p class="lead">As financial AI moves from analyzing cases to initiating actions, tool access cannot be treated as blanket authority. BeaconGuard checks the exact business effect before execution.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Consequential actions</h2>
    <div class="section-grid section-grid--compact">
      <div class="content-card"><h3>Case disposition</h3><p>Authorize the exact AML/KYC, fraud, or dispute workflow change before case state changes.</p></div>
      <div class="content-card"><h3>Customer communication</h3><p>Authorize the exact outbound communication before it reaches the customer.</p></div>
      <div class="content-card"><h3>Account or workflow action</h3><p>Authorize the exact downstream side effect before it touches the operational platform.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What BeaconGuard does not replace</h2>
    <p>Compliance judgment, analyst authority, transaction systems, identity, and systems of record remain authoritative. BeaconGuard enforces the exact-action authorization boundary those authorities require.</p>
    <div class="page-actions"><a class="btn-primary" href="/design-partner-program">Evaluate a Financial Workflow</a><a class="btn-secondary" href="/trust-assurance">Review Assurance</a></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
